                <pb facs="0518" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 22372/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul
                    Caldera.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox instructs Mr. Caldera to ascertain immediately and telegraph the
                    department fully positive information as to the fate of the two captured
                    Americans. Says the Government of the United States can scarcely credit the
                    report of the summary execution of two Americans taken with the revolutionary
                    army. Mr. Knox says further that the Nicaraguan chargé d’affaires in Washington
                    has been asked to demand telegraphically full information for this Government
                    which will not for one moment tolerate such treatment of American citizens.</p>
            </div>
